							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left"><div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1506.msg17248#msg17248">Quote from: Kkhaarn on May 24, 2005, 11:12:15 pm</a></div><div class="quote">i mean why bring shit up like this? are you bored? waiting on a raid and cant think of anything else to do? have some deep seeded hatred for DN and it just finally got the best of you? an officer of a highend raiding guild should know how to better contol themselves in the public view.<br /></div><br />Bored?&nbsp; Ya, kinda.&nbsp; I&#039;m quitting EQ actually - so I sort of have nothing to loose.&nbsp; I&#039;ve known about all the bullshit with DN for quite some time but never called them out for basically that reason - public appearances had to be kept up.&nbsp; But I don&#039;t care about those anymore.&nbsp; <br /><br />As for calling me a hypocrite - perhaps am I.&nbsp; I remember now where all this is comming from.&nbsp; Vex Thall - I was leading a small raid bouncing from target to target killing the named for fun on an offnight.&nbsp; I noticed you zone in with a group of fizzle fiends players (not sure if you were just boxing them all) and watched you warp to DXVT and kill him.&nbsp; You probibly noticed us in the zone as well, and of course saw what I was doing using your own means.&nbsp; So tell me, does being a &quot;hacker&quot; while calling me out for hacking while calling someone else out for hacking constitue as being a hypocrite as well?<br /><br />Also, I must disagree with you that cheating is cheating no matter what one is doing.&nbsp; Using MQ to check if a mob is up to expediate the calling of raid targets and using it to make yourself invincible are two totally different things.&nbsp; In one instance you are saving your guild a little time, in another you are physically defeating content that would otherwise defeat you.&nbsp; Don&#039;t make me break out the bad analogies...<br /><br />And